          "total_marks": 3,
          "stem_markdown": "The height of a certain species of plant is denoted by \\(H\\) cm. The heights of a random sample of 100 plants were measured, and the following results were found.\n\n- The mean, \\(\\bar{h}\\), for the sample was 80.2.\n- An unbiased estimate of the population variance of \\(H\\) was 15.6.\n\nCalculate the value of \\(\\Sigma h^2\\).",
          "question_number": 2,
          "mark_scheme_items": [
            {
              "mark_code": "M1",
              "part_path": [],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 1,
              "content_markdown": "$$15.6 = \\frac{100}{99} \\left( \\frac{\\Sigma h^2}{100} - 80.2^2 \\right)$$ OR $$15.6 = 1/99 \\left( \\Sigma h^2 - 8020^2/100 \\right)$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "For attempt biased or unbiased = 15.6.",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                9
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "A1",
              "part_path": [],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 2,
              "content_markdown": "",
              "guidance_markdown": "For correct expression = 15.6.",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                9
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "A1",
              "part_path": [],
              "is_final_answer": true,
              "sequence_number": 3,
              "content_markdown": "$$\\Sigma h^2 = 644748.4$$ or $$645000 \\text{ (3 sf)}$$ or $$3223742/5$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                9
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            }
          ],
          "source_page_numbers": [
            4
