            "taxonomy_version": "cambridge-maths-v1",
            "calculator_required": null,
            "classification_confidence": 0.8
          },
          "total_marks": 4,
          "stem_markdown": "A biased spinner has four sides. Each side is of a different colour: yellow, red, green or black. The probability, \\(p\\), that the spinner will land on red is unknown. The spinner was spun 200 times, and the proportion, \\(a\\), of times that it landed on red was noted. This proportion was used to calculate an approximate 90% confidence interval for \\(p\\). The width of this confidence interval was 0.1066 correct to 4 significant figures.\n\nFind the two possible values of \\(a\\).",
          "question_number": 4,
          "mark_scheme_items": [
            {
              "mark_code": "M1",
              "part_path": [],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 1,
              "content_markdown": "$$2 \\times 1.645 \\times \\sqrt{\\frac{a(1-a)}{200}} = 0.1066$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "Allow any $$z$$ and/or omit ‘$$2 \\times$$’. Condone confusion between $$a$$ and $$\\frac{a}{200}$$. E.g. $$2 \\times 1.645 \\times \\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{a}{200}\\left(1-\\frac{a}{200}\\right)}{200}} = 0.1066$$",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                11
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "B1",
              "part_path": [],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 2,
              "content_markdown": "$$z = 1.645$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                11
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "M1",
              "part_path": [],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 3,
              "content_markdown": "$$a^2 - a + 0.20997 = 0$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "Or for valid attempt to reach quadratic in $$a$$ by confusing between $$a$$ and $$\\left(\\frac{a}{200}\\right)$$. E.g. $$a^2 - 200a + 8398.7 = 0$$",
